      "writtenOn": "2023-11-08T11:47:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "in the comment above it is stayed \"as defined by Pacs\"\n\nIt is actually defined by Assigned Numbers and in Assigned numbers it says \"values\"\n\nhttps://btprodspecificationrefs.blob.core.windows.net/assigned-numbers/Assigned%20Number%20Types/Assigned_Numbers.pdf\n\n6.12.3 Context Type",
      "parentUuid": "3b0949ee_7ebba6a4",
      "revId": "0aeb259e8c831ab0d67b3f556e51dff6ee31fd69",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a0ac11ae_89a985c0",
        "filename": "bluetooth/audio/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/audio/AudioContext.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1899057
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-08T17:31:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "PACS define the characteristic and the behavior, Assigned number define the values. In PACS (3.5), we can read `Bitmask of audio data Context Type values...`, and the values are defined in a way to do a bitmask.\n\nI think the conversion is better in this way, and makes the code more readable.\n\nBy the way, as it doesn\u0027t looks as clear as wanted, and this also have issues regarding equivalence (if we do not fix order in the array). I propose to change it to parcelable of boolean. I also think, this will always be used as a bitmask, so looks better too.\n\nDoes that makes sense?",
      "parentUuid": "aa161f0c_41c58761",
      "revId": "0aeb259e8c831ab0d67b3f556e51dff6ee31fd69",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
